{"id": "EUVD-2026-83882", "enisaUuid": "4f53ad47-5bfa-3101-92af-4d7f177fed97", "description": "In Eclipse iceoryx2 versions greater than v0.8.0, the StaticString exposes its contents as mutable bytes through safe APIs, while String::as_str() converts those bytes into a Rust string slice without validating UTF-8. An application can therefore create an invalid &str and trigger undefined behavior using entirely safe Rust.", "datePublished": "2026-09-21T10:47:02", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-21T11:09:34", "baseScore": 1.0, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:H/AT:P/PR:H/UI:A/VC:N/VI:L/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/eclipse-iceoryx/iceoryx2/security/advisories/GHSA-8mq4-3mwq-qvg6", "https://gitlab.eclipse.org/security/cve-assignment/-/work_items/307", "https://github.com/eclipse-iceoryx/iceoryx2/releases/tag/v0.10.0", "https://crates.io/crates/iceoryx2-bb-container/0.10.0"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-92612", "GHSA-gm83-3hcx-j6jj"], "assigner": "eclipse", "epss": 0.15, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "db794285-bcd5-3fbd-b999-d769fa4535c2", "product": {"name": "Eclipse iceoryx\u2122", "vendor": {"name": "Eclipse Foundation"}}, "product_version": "0.8.1 \u2264*"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "a9cd678c-79ec-3865-a4c4-c9c655ee4bf2", "vendor": {"name": "Eclipse Foundation"}}], "isExploited": false}